@startuml j9-model-blocked
!include c4-sequence.iuml
title J9 The run with the model blocked
actor "Patient" as Patient <<person>>
box "In the patient's browser"
participant "Patient chat\n(chat.js)" as Chat <<container>>
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core <<component>>
database "Browser storage\n(localStorage)" as LS <<store>>
end box
box "Vercel functions"
participant "api/chat.js" as Api <<container>>
end box
participant "OpenRouter" as OR <<external>>

Patient -> Chat : taps "Timings"
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(question,\nclinic file, language)
Core --> Chat : the draft answer and\nthe facts it holds
note over Core, Api : The rules engine always answers first;\nthe model may only reword the draft.
Chat -> Api : POST /api/chat (the draft,\nits facts, the language,\nthe clinic file)
alt the request is blocked, or no reply within 9 seconds
  Chat -> Chat : gives up waiting
else no model key on the server
  Api --> Chat : 503 "no key"
else the model fails or is slow
  Api -> OR : reword the draft\n(one try, 8 seconds)
  Api --> Chat : 502 or 504
else the reworded text breaks a rule of the guard
  Api -> Api : FD.guard rejects the text
  Api --> Chat : 422 "failed the check"
end
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket (question,\nthe draft as the reply)
Core -> LS : the ticket joins\nthis browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : the draft, with "Answered\nfrom the clinic file" under it
note right of Patient : the patient always gets\nan answer from the file
@enduml
